# RTK Shell Usage (Always On)

**Type:** Strict rule

## Required Behavior

- **Always run shell commands through `rtk` (including `git` and `gh`)** to reduce output noise and keep logs token-efficient.
- **Keep the existing monorepo `cd $(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/... &&` prefix rule** from `Directory Execution Constraints`.
- **Only exception**: **repo-root typecheck must be `pnpm typecheck` (no `rtk`)**, per `docs/rtk-reference.md`.

## Key Patterns

```bash
# Repo root
cd $(git rev-parse --show-toplevel) && rtk pnpm install

# Backend
cd $(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/apps/backend && rtk pnpm dev
cd $(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/apps/backend && rtk pnpm test

# Frontend
cd $(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/apps/frontend && rtk pnpm dev
cd $(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/apps/frontend && rtk pnpm test

# Git / GitHub
cd $(git rev-parse --show-toplevel) && rtk git status
cd $(git rev-parse --show-toplevel) && rtk gh pr view 123

# Exception: repo-root typecheck (no rtk)
cd $(git rev-parse --show-toplevel) && pnpm typecheck
```

## Prohibited Patterns

- ❌ Running `pnpm`, `git`, `gh`, `docker`, `kubectl`, test runners, or other CLI tools without `rtk` when `rtk` passthrough is available.
- ❌ Mixing wrapped and unwrapped commands in a chain (prefer `rtk ... && rtk ...`).

## Failure Debugging

If `rtk` output is too filtered to diagnose a failure, **read the RTK tee log** as documented in `docs/rtk-reference.md` instead of re-running the command repeatedly.
